# Validation 6: a Builder wish for another mod's item, and that item working in a Moddy world. The Wish Builder's
# Supplies page has a 🔍 Find that searches every installed item by name, mods included; here it finds The Last Sword
# (the reforged one, the_last_sword:the_last_sword, from the mod of the same name, with its library Epic Core API),
# the Builder makes it, and the sword the player was given kills a
# Warden, the hardest vanilla mob (500 health), by melee.
@intent A Builder wish finds The Last Sword by name and gives it, and that sword kills a Warden

@step a clear stage
gamemode creative
time set noon
weather clear
gamerule doDaylightCycle false
gamerule doMobSpawning false
execute if entity @e[type=!minecraft:player] run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 10

@step find The Last Sword in the Builder's supplies
/moddy builder
@expect screen Wish Builder within 10s
@click item "Supplies"
@expect screen What do you need within 5s
@click item "Find"
@expect screen /find/ within 5s
@type "last sword"
@shot find-box
@click button "Find it!"
@expect screen Is it one of these within 15s
@shot found

@step the Builder makes it
@click item "Last Sword"
@wait 1s
@shot after-pick
@click button "Make it!"
@expect chat /getting .*last sword/ within 30s
# Moddy delivers it with a short show (a beam, a boss bar), then says where it went: "The Last Sword is in slot 3!".
@expect chat /last sword is in slot/ within 90s
@repeat 10 until execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:the_last_sword
@wait 1s
@end-repeat
@assert execute if items entity @s container.* the_last_sword:the_last_sword
@shot got-the-sword

@step a Warden to fight
# Moddy said "in slot 3": the first free hotbar slot (the watch and the wish bag hold the first two).
@key key.hotbar.3
@assert execute if items entity @s weapon.mainhand the_last_sword:the_last_sword
summon minecraft:warden ~ ~ ~6 {NoAI:1b}
@assert execute if entity @e[type=minecraft:warden,distance=..16]
@aim entity minecraft:warden
@shot the-warden

@step the sword kills it
@repeat each @e[type=minecraft:warden,distance=..32] max 40 until execute unless entity {it}
execute at @s rotated as @s rotated ~ 0 run tp {it} ^ ^ ^2
@wait 5t
@aim entity {it}
@key key.attack
@wait 12t
@end-repeat
@wait 2s
@assert execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:warden,distance=..64]
@shot warden-defeated
